# Build context for mcp/Dockerfile, whose context is this workspace root (see its header).
#
# `node_modules` is the line that matters. Without it the context is the developer's INSTALLED
# tree — hundreds of MB, and on Apple silicon it carries the darwin-arm64 native binaries of
# oxlint, rolldown and lightningcss into a linux/amd64 build. The `npm ci` in the build stage
# would then be layered on top of a tree it did not create, so the image's dependencies would
# depend on the machine that ran the build.
**/node_modules

# The build stage emits these itself. Copying a local `dist/` in is exactly how §139's build-order
# defect stayed hidden — it passed on a developer's machine because a previous run had left one
# behind — so the image must never be able to see one.
**/dist

# Test scratch, editor state, and the caches vitest leaves inside each workspace member.
**/.vite
**/.vite-temp
**/.tmp
**/coverage
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
